  "findings": [
    "Default hyperparameters agree: 1.6.1 first grid point n_estimators=50, max_depth=4, min_samples_split=2, min_samples_leaf=1 (grid min_samples_split 2/6, min_samples_leaf 1/3); v2 declares n_estimators=50, max_depth=4 and the non-tunable min_samples_split=2, min_samples_leaf=1, learning_rate=1.0 (sklearn's default, which 1.6.1 leaves implicit).",
    "Neither side pins `random_state`, so the boosting is reproducible only through the global numpy seed. Reproducing a v2 run requires the caller to seed numpy; B5 may want to pin a `random_state` on both models.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset consumes the whole gene expression view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`). The case compares a pre-selected matrix; wiring the list into the preset belongs to B5.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64. The boosting rounds are identical (same estimator weights and errors) because the trees see the same split order."
